  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0223 database is designed to manage information about candidates, positions, users, and voters in an election process. The Candidate table stores details about each candidate, including their name, service ID, designation, workplace, mobile number, email, and photo path. The CandidatePosition table links candidates to specific positions, with each record referencing a candidate's ID and a position's ID. The Position table contains information about each position, including its name and the number of posts available. The Role table defines different roles, such as the type of role, and is linked to the User table, which stores details about each user, including their name, service ID, mobile number, email, password, and role ID. The VoteCastingInformation table tracks voting information, referencing the candidate's ID, the voter's ID, and the position ID. The Voter table stores details about each voter, including their name, service ID, mobile number, email, blood group, whether they have been selected, whether their vote has been committed, a unique identification number, and whether a mail has been sent to them. The database ensures data integrity through various constraints, such as primary keys in each table, unique constraints in the Voter table, and foreign keys that link tables together, with some referencing other tables with ON DELETE CASCADE rules to ensure that related records are deleted when necessary, while others have ON DELETE RESTRICT rules to prevent deletion of referenced records.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\nThe project involves the development of an online voting system designed to streamline the electoral process. The system will facilitate electronic voting by providing functionalities for managing candidates and voters, casting votes, and displaying results in real-time.\n\n Objectives\n- Implement a secure and user-friendly online voting platform.\n- Allow authorized voters to cast their votes efficiently and accurately.\n- Provide election administrators with tools to manage candidates and voter information.\n- Ensure real-time display of voting results upon election closure.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n- Election Administrators: Manage candidate and voter lists, oversee the voting process.\n- Voters: Registered users who can cast votes in the election.\n- Candidates: Individuals running for positions in the election.\n- System Developers/IT Personnel: Maintain and support the system infrastructure.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n1. Candidate Management:\n   - Maintain a list of candidates including details such as name, designation, workplace, contact information, and photo.\n   - Assign candidates to specific positions available for election.\n\n2. Voter Management:\n   - Maintain a list of registered voters with personal and contact information.\n   - Track whether voters have committed their vote and manage their voting eligibility.\n\n3. Vote Casting:\n   - Provide a secure panel for voters to cast their votes for available positions.\n   - Ensure votes are accurately recorded against each candidate.\n\n4. Voting Results:\n   - Display election results by aggregating votes for each position.\n   - Update results in real-time as votes are cast.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Security: Ensure data integrity and confidentiality through encryption and secure authentication mechanisms.\n- Performance: Support up to a predetermined number of concurrent users without compromising system speed or accuracy.\n- Scalability: Allow for future expansion to support additional users, candidates, and election types.\n- Usability: Design intuitive user interfaces accessible to individuals with varying levels of technical expertise.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0223.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0223\nCREATE TABLE `candidate` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `service_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `designation` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `workplace` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `mobile_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `photo_path` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `position` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_posts` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `candidate_position` (\n  `candidate_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `position_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`candidate_id`, `position_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `candidate_position_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`candidate_id`) REFERENCES `candidate` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `candidate_position_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`position_id`) REFERENCES `position` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `role_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `service_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `mobile_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role` (`id`) ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `voter` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `service_id` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `mobile_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `blood_group` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `is_selected` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `vote_committed` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `unique_identification_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  `mail_sent` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `vote_casting_information` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `candidate_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `voter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `position_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `vote_casting_information_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`candidate_id`) REFERENCES `candidate` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `vote_casting_information_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`voter_id`) REFERENCES `voter` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `vote_casting_information_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`position_id`) REFERENCES `position` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
